  "id": "DrugBank_DB14640 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Isoflupredone Acetate may be a potential repurposed drug for Vasomotor Rhinitis, as it is associated with Allergic Rhinitis, which in turn is linked to Vasomotor Rhinitis through multiple pathways. The core mechanism appears to involve the treatment of Allergic Rhinitis, a condition that is often associated with vasomotor symptoms, and the repurposing of Isoflupredone Acetate to target this condition. The evidence is supported by the presence of multiple indications that connect Isoflupredone Acetate to Vasomotor Rhinitis, with the shared pathway of Allergic Rhinitis acting as a bridge. The mechanisms likely involve the modulation of inflammatory or neurogenic pathways that contribute to vasomotor rhinitis, though the exact molecular targets remain to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Isoflupredone Acetate may exert a therapeutic effect on Vasomotor Rhinitis through its interaction with the immune or neurogenic system, though further mechanistic validation is required to confirm this relationship.",
